# Skill Router

On every prompt, classify the task and READ + FOLLOW the matched skill file(s) before doing the work. Skills live at `/Users/lunar/.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`.

## Task → Skill

- Writing/updating docs or the wiki → `documentation-writer` AND `obsidian-markdown`. Also obey `wiki-contract.mdc`.
- Editing any `.md` in `wiki/` → `obsidian-markdown` (wikilinks, frontmatter, callouts).
- Tracking tasks / "what's on my plate" → `task-management` (`TASKS.md`).
- Remember / glossary / people / preferences → `memory-management` (`CLAUDE.md`, `memory/`).
- Multi-step feature before code → `brainstorming` then `writing-plans` (save under `docs/superpowers/plans/`).
- Executing an existing plan → `executing-plans` or `subagent-driven-development`.
- Building/refactoring UI → `impeccable` (and design passes: `critique`, `polish`, `layout`, etc. as needed).
- TypeScript/API work → `typescript-expert` when types or architecture get hard.
- Bug fixes → `systematic-debugging` first.
- Done / verify → `verification-before-completion`.

## Stack-specific

- API under `apps/api/` → follow `clean-architecture.mdc` + `stack-conventions.mdc` (Full CA)
- Web under `apps/web/` → Full CA presentation only: page → hook → API client; never import domain/application
- Schema / migrations → Drizzle under `apps/api/src/infrastructure/db`; never mutate stock without movements
- Any Phase A–F feature work → Clean Architecture layers; see `docs/architecture/coding-standards.md`

## Rules

- Multiple skills can apply at once
- If no skill matches, proceed normally
- Do not just mention a skill — read it and apply it
